614
00:20:36,890 --> 00:20:38,320
Takaba!

615
00:20:38,970 --> 00:20:41,130
How long are ya gonna
keep doin' that crap?!

616
00:20:41,130 --> 00:20:42,670
Cut it out!

617
00:20:42,670 --> 00:20:44,880
You're making me depressed, too!

618
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:46,270
Yeah.

619
00:20:47,610 --> 00:20:49,350
How old are ya now?

620
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:51,270
Thirty-five!

621
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:53,400
Then give it up already.

622
00:20:53,400 --> 00:21:00,120
Our industry's full o' late-bloomers who
suddenly make it big for no good reason,

623
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,950
but none of 'em suddenly got funnier.

624
00:21:02,950 --> 00:21:06,270
They were just funny people
waiting to be discovered.

625
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:09,010
And that ain't the case for you!

626
00:21:09,430 --> 00:21:11,430
Look what happened to Tokyo.

627
00:21:11,430 --> 00:21:12,780
No one's gonna think ill of you.

628
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:15,230
Go do something you're actually suited for.

629
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:21,910
I never disliked your comedy, Takaba.

630
00:21:23,830 --> 00:21:25,000
Ken-san?

631
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,410
Both you and him have the wrong idea.

632
00:21:28,250 --> 00:21:31,210
There's still people who ain't
funny that make it big.

633
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:37,120
You mean those with one stock gag?

634
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,030
Nah.

635
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:40,680
There are two types of comedians
that manage to stay big.

636
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,160
Comedians who are always funny,

637
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:47,180
and comedians who can always delude
themselves into believing they're funny.

638
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:56,000
Which one are you?

639
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:00,400
I'd say it's 50-50,
but it's actually 70-30...

640
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,630
50-50...

641
00:22:01,630 --> 00:22:03,880
I'd say it's 50-50,

642
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:09,970
Culling Game Player
Fumihiko Takaba

643
00:22:04,190 --> 00:22:06,710
but it's actually 70-30!

644
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,440
Mai, I'll get started.

645
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,820
Why did you come here?

646
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:45,740
Shall I bully you like I used to?

647
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:47,410
Then, please, you do it, Maki-san.

648
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:49,300
You are me, and I am you.

649
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:50,740
Make me happy I gave birth to you.

650
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:52,320
Absolutely ridiculous.

651
00:23:51,610 --> 00:23:53,820
Destroy it all.

652
